Subject: [PATCH 163/174] docs: film grain specification for the cinematic
 camera

Replaces CE's stock film grain for ccam with a capture-side noise model: a
shared skeleton (calibrated display-domain blend after the temporal resolve,
film-mm coordinates, stateless seeding from a ccam-owned capture-frame
counter), a film family (offline-synthesised grain plates) and a digital
family (shot + read + fixed-pattern sensor model with CMOS / CCD / Phone
variants). Stock behaviour stays byte-identical when the block is inactive.
Stages G0-G3, one agent each.

